  "answer_text": "While I cannot directly book or purchase tickets for you because I do not have access to your payment details or personal information, I can guide you through the process and provide the direct links to secure your ticket.\n\n### 1. Identify Your Dates\nDepending on how you phrase it, \"next Friday\" could refer to:\n* **Friday, June 12, 2026** (the upcoming Friday)\n* **Friday, June 19, 2026** (the following Friday)\n\nBecause you requested a **return (round-trip)** ticket, you will also need to select your return date (for example, the following Sunday, June 14 or June 21).\n\n### 2. How to Book Your Tickets\nYou can purchase your tickets directly through [Amtrak's Official Website](https://www.amtrak.com/) or via the Amtrak mobile app. \n\nWhen booking, use the following details:\n* **From:** Boston, MA - South Station (BOS) or Back Bay (BBY)\n* **To:** New York, NY - Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)\n* **Trip Type:** Round Trip\n* **Depart Date:** June 12, 2026 (or June 19, 2026)\n* **Return Date:** *[Select your preferred return date]*\n\n### 3. Choose Your Train Service\nAmtrak offers two main services for this route:\n* **Northeast Regional:** Takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. This is the standard, more affordable option.\n* **Acela:** Takes about **3 hours and 30 minutes**. This is Amtrak's high-speed, premium option consisting of only Business and First Class seating.\n\n---\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Important Travel Alert for Boston Travelers (June \u2013 July 2026):**\nPlease note that due to the 2026 World Cup, there is an active alert impacting access to Boston South Station from **June 11 to July 9, 2026**. Be sure to check [Amtrak's Train Status](https://www.amtrak.com/) before you depart and plan to arrive at the station earlier than usual to account for any security or crowd delays!",
